# Why this file exists: on other people's machines the one-click launchers used to
# die with "'cho' / 'neq' / 噺部署 is not recognized ...".  Two things caused it:
#   1) UTF-8 Chinese bytes inside a .bat + `chcp 65001` run from the same file makes
#      cmd.exe desync its own batch read offset (it resumes mid-line).
#   2) core.autocrlf only fixes `git clone`; GitHub's "Download ZIP" hands out the
#      stored blob as-is, so every ZIP user got a different byte layout than the dev.
# The launchers are now pure ASCII (Chinese comes from Python), and `-text` below
# freezes their exact CRLF bytes into the repository so clone and ZIP agree.
* text=auto

# Ship these byte-for-byte, no EOL conversion in either direction.
*.bat  -text
*.cmd  -text
*.vbs  -text
*.ps1  -text

*.py    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
